<h2 id="capability-areas">Capability areas</h2>
<p class="wp-p"><strong>Catalog and merchandising</strong> — Flexible attribute models, category rules, and staging for seasonal campaigns. Integrate PIM when SKU complexity exceeds native admin efficiency.</p>
<p class="wp-p"><strong>Checkout and payments</strong> — Optimize for mobile, support vaulted payments, and localize tax/shipping. B2B flows require approval chains and purchase order support.</p>
<p class="wp-p"><strong>Integrations</strong> — ERP for inventory and invoicing, CRM for customer history, and marketing automation for lifecycle campaigns. Prefer APIs and async jobs over brittle point-to-point scripts.</p>

<h2 id="implementation-roadmap">Implementation roadmap</h2>
<p class="wp-p">Phase 1: Baseline performance, security patches, and analytics. Phase 2: Catalog cleanup and search relevance. Phase 3: B2B or international expansion. Phase 4: Headless storefronts or PWA where channel strategy requires it.</p>

